From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 01:26:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: pcie: say why the ring indices fall back to
 TCM

When the firmware offers DMA'd ring indices (BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_DMA_INDEX)
but the index buffer cannot be allocated, brcmfmac quietly uses the
indices in device memory instead, which hides a DMA setup problem and
makes every ring update a PCIe read. Log the fallback as an error, and
log the shared-area flags at PCIe debug level so the firmware's
capabilities can be read from a debug log.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
index c9431c81e..b4f7d9038 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/pcie.c
@@ -1473,8 +1473,10 @@ static int brcmf_pcie_init_ringbuffers(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo)
 		devinfo->idxbuf = dma_alloc_coherent(&devinfo->pdev->dev, bufsz,
 						     &devinfo->idxbuf_dmahandle,
 						     GFP_KERNEL);
-		if (!devinfo->idxbuf)
+		if (!devinfo->idxbuf) {
+			brcmf_err(bus, "no DMA memory for ring indices, using TCM\n");
 			devinfo->dma_idx_sz = 0;
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (devinfo->dma_idx_sz == 0) {
@@ -1848,6 +1850,7 @@ brcmf_pcie_init_share_ram_info(struct brcmf_pciedev_info *devinfo,
 
 	shared->flags = brcmf_pcie_read_tcm32(devinfo, sharedram_addr);
 	shared->version = (u8)(shared->flags & BRCMF_PCIE_SHARED_VERSION_MASK);
+	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "shared flags 0x%08x\n", shared->flags);
 	brcmf_dbg(PCIE, "PCIe protocol version %d\n", shared->version);
 	if ((shared->version > BRCMF_PCIE_MAX_SHARED_VERSION) ||
 	    (shared->version < BRCMF_PCIE_MIN_SHARED_VERSION)) {
